# Append-only files written by the bot, merged with git's built-in "union"
# driver: on conflict, keep BOTH sides' lines instead of failing.
#
# Why this is needed: two workflow jobs can each append to the same day's
# log (GitHub lets a queued job start as the previous one is finishing),
# both starting from the same commit. Git cannot auto-merge two different
# appends to the end of one file -- it's a textbook conflict -- so the
# rebase in the commit step failed and the whole step failed with it.
#
# Measured on 2026-07-27: 2 of 5 runs failed that way, and 150 minutes of
# trading log plus some trades.csv rows were permanently lost. That is
# the exact evidence these files exist to preserve, so losing it silently
# is the worst possible failure for them.
#
# "union" is the standard answer for changelog-style files. Worst case it
# duplicates a line; it never drops one, and it never conflicts.
logs/*.log merge=union
trades.csv merge=union
